Error [E0201]: An ExpiringSecret loan cannot be stored
  --> expiring_secret_requires_ownership_and_rejects_loan_escape_4.jet:12:18
    |
 12 |         saved := [borrowed]
    |                  ^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: The callback parameter is a temporary read-only loan that ends when `.with` returns
 Fix: Use the loan inside the callback and store only a non-secret result
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0201

Error [E0113]: `run` doesn't return a value
  --> expiring_secret_requires_ownership_and_rejects_loan_escape_4.jet:13:16
    |
 13 |         return saved
    |                ^^^^^
 Why: A function hands back a value only when it declares a return type
 Fix: Remove the value (a bare `return`), or write `-> [<corelib>/core.crypto::SigningKey]` after the parameter list
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0113

Error [E0201]: An ExpiringSecret loan cannot escape its callback
  --> expiring_secret_requires_ownership_and_rejects_loan_escape_4.jet:11:17
    |
 11 |     _ := secret.with((borrowed) -> {
    |                 ^^^^
 Why: The callback receives a temporary read-only loan; returning a secret would create another owned credential outside the expiry boundary
 Fix: Return a non-secret result such as a signature, public key, status, or response
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0201

Error [E2402]: This implicit fallible call can't convert `Expired` into `Err` — no declared conversion exists
  --> expiring_secret_requires_ownership_and_rejects_loan_escape_4.jet:11:17
    |
 11 |     _ := secret.with((borrowed) -> {
    |                 ^^^^
 Why: Ordinary fallible calls propagate automatically; `Expired` can reach `Err` only through `impl Expired -> Err`
 Fix: Handle this call locally with `??`, add `impl Expired -> Err { … }`, or change the return type
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2402
